# Medical: aligned to NHS practice in England. Sourced by mg-install. [NFR-SEC-1] [NFR-PRV-1]
PROFILE_TITLE="Healthcare (NHS aligned)"
PROFILE_SUMMARY="NHS organisations by ODS code, care units by treatment function, pseudonymised patients, encounters coded in SNOMED CT, referrals with RTT clocks, a DCB0129 / DCB0160 hazard log and Caldicott reviews. Local AI on the Granite model."
PROFILE_COMPONENTS="forge mimir"
PROFILE_MODEL=granite
PROFILE_TOTP=required
PROFILE_ADMINS=2
PROFILE_CLEARANCE=confidential
PROFILE_PURPOSES=operations,direct-care
PROFILE_TIER=M
PROFILE_SAMPLES=""
PROFILE_FEEDS=""
PROFILE_NOTES=(
  "Health data is special category data (UK GDPR Article 9 and the Data Protection Act 2018). Complete a DPIA and include the system in your Data Security and Protection Toolkit submission before live use."
  "Load pseudonymised data only. The schema has no name, address or NHS number fields by design; re-identification stays in the source system."
  "DCB0129 (manufacturers) and DCB0160 (deploying organisations) apply to health IT; the hazard log is there for your clinical safety officer. Midgard is not a medical device and has no clinical safety case: its output is not for clinical decisions."
  "Record Caldicott Guardian decisions on new uses of data. The national data opt-out applies to uses beyond individual care."
  "Codes follow NHS standards: ODS codes, treatment function codes and SNOMED CT. Keep records for the periods in the NHS Records Management Code of Practice."
  "Two administrators are created for dual control. Hand each passkey file to its owner and remove it from this server."
)
